# Skill: handoff

Cursor adapter for the `handoff` skill. Full procedure (single source of truth):
`.claude/skills/handoff/SKILL.md` in this repo.

## When To Use

Session is ending and the paper-work context should be frozen for next time. One context only:
finishing the HESS dataset paper.

## When Not To Use

A quick mid-session checkpoint (use `/save`).

## Workflow

Capture current paper state + next steps + known debt into a single living `project`-type auto-memory
entry under `~/.claude/projects/-home-dmbrmv-Development-camels-ru/memory/` (prefer updating the
existing paper-state memory; refresh the `MEMORY.md` index). Check git (`git status -sb` parent,
`git -C paper/overleaf status -s` manuscript) and note the state. Suggest a commit if there are
uncommitted changes.

## Output Handling

Print a short confirmation: auto-memory file updated, git state (parent + manuscript) with a suggested
commit message if dirty, and the concrete "pick up from" next action.

## Safety Constraints

No auto-commit, no force push — the user commits. No manuscript edits to record the handoff. No
invented session/initiative trees — only auto-memory and git.
